{#- servers: NTP= for systemd-timesyncd. Empty default: without pillar the
   drop-in sets nothing and timesyncd keeps Debian's behaviour.

   fallback_servers: FallbackNTP=. Empty on purpose (an empty assignment
   clears Debian's debian.pool.ntp.org default): with one internal source
   every VM is wrong *together* if that source is wrong, instead of a VM
   that can't reach it drifting off onto the public pool.

   Per-link servers from DHCP (systemd-networkd) are still used alongside
   NTP= — on this network that's the same FRITZ!Box via IPv6. #}
{%- set defaults = {
    'pkg': 'systemd-timesyncd',
    'service': 'systemd-timesyncd',
    'dropin': '/etc/systemd/timesyncd.conf.d/salt.conf',
    'servers': [],
    'fallback_servers': [],
} %}
{%- set ntp = salt['pillar.get']('ntp:lookup', default=defaults, merge=True) %}
